{"_ts": 1788893226.8100736, "url": "https://littlesis.org/api/entities/2036/connections?category_id=1", "body": {"meta": {"copyright": "LittleSis CC BY-SA 4.0", "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "apiVersion": "2.0"}, "data": [{"type": "entities", "id": 39, "attributes": {"id": 39, "name": "RTX", "blurb": "The world's second-largest aerospace-and-defense company", "summary": "Publicly-traded defense and aerospace contractor, the result of mergers by UTC and Raytheon and the spin-offs of Otis Worldwide and Carrier ", "website": "https://www.rtx.com", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2025-05-21T16:59:25Z", "start_date": "1934-00-00", "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "1420411", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["IRS EIN 06-0570975", "RTX", "Raytheon Technologies", "Raytheon Technologies Corporation", "United Technologies", "United Technologies Corporation"], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "United Technologies", "name_nick": "UNITED_TECH", "employees": null, "revenue": 56098000000, "fedspending_id": "327319", "lda_registrant_id": "39267"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "RTX", "sec_cik": 101829}}, "tags": ["corporate-mapping-project", "fossil-fuel-industry", "corpu", "corpu-possible-duplicates"]}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/39-RTX"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 15016, "attributes": {"id": 15016, "name": "University of Miami", "blurb": "Private research university in Coral Gables, Florida", "summary": "Established in 1925 during the region\u2019s famous real estate boom, UM is a major research university engaged in $360 million in research and sponsored program expenditures a year. While the majority of this work is housed at the Miller School of Medicine. \r\n\r\nThe University comprises 12 schools and colleges serving undergraduate and graduate students in more than 180 majors and programs.", "website": "https://welcome.miami.edu/", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2024-12-07T18:04:04Z", "start_date": "1925-00-00", "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "606388", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["University of Miami"], "types": ["Organization", "School"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "University of Miami", "name_nick": null, "employees": null, "revenue": null, "fedspending_id": null, "lda_registrant_id": null}, "School": {"endowment": null, "students": null, "faculty": null, "tuition": null, "is_private": null}}, "tags": []}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/15016-University_of_Miami"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 64, "attributes": {"id": 64, "name": "Mondel\u0113z International, Inc.", "blurb": "Manufactures consumer food products", "summary": null, "website": "http://www.kraft.com", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2025-09-19T15:29:11Z", "start_date": null, "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "1748570,1417", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["IRS EIN 52-2884372", "Kraft Food", "Kraft Foods", "Kraft Foods Inc.", "Kraft General Foods Corporation", "Mondelez Int", "Mondelez International", "Mondelez International, Inc.", "Mondel\u0113z International, Inc."], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "Mondel\u0113z International, Inc.", "name_nick": "MONDELEZ_INT", "employees": null, "revenue": 37241000000, "fedspending_id": "369350", "lda_registrant_id": "314192"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "KFT", "sec_cik": 1103982}}, "tags": ["buffalo", "corporate-mapping-project", "corpu"]}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/64-Mondel%C4%93z_International,_Inc."}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 78, "attributes": {"id": 78, "name": "Hess Corporation", "blurb": "Oil and Gas Operations", "summary": null, "website": "www.hess.com", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2025-07-29T07:11:50Z", "start_date": "1920-00-00", "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "564756", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["Amerada Corporation", "Amerada Hess", "Amerada Hess Corporation", "Amerada Petroleum Corporation", "Hess", "Hess Corporation", "Hess Energy", "IRS EIN 13-4921002"], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "Hess Corporation", "name_nick": "HESS", "employees": null, "revenue": 6510000000, "fedspending_id": "145029", "lda_registrant_id": "66352"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "HES", "sec_cik": 4447}}, "tags": ["fracking", "corporate-mapping-project"]}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/78-Hess_Corporation"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 192, "attributes": {"id": 192, "name": "Paramount Global", "blurb": "On December 4, 2019, Viacom Inc. merged into CBS Corporation; on February 16 2022 the combined company was renamed Paramount", "summary": "By 2023 Paramount Global emerged as an archetype for the media industry\u2019s consolidation conundrum. The company consists of Paramount Pictures, the CBS broadcast network, 28 owned-and-operated local CBS stations, the streaming service Paramount+, free advertising-supported Pluto TV, \u201cStar Trek,\u201d \u201cSpongeBob SquarePants,\u201d MTV, Nickelodeon, Comedy Central, BET and Showtime. It also owns the physical Paramount studio lot in Los Angeles, California.\r\n\r\nViacom Inc. was an American multinational media conglomerate with interests primarily in cinema and cable television. It was the world's sixth largest broadcasting and cable company in terms of revenue.\r\n\r\nCBS and Viacom merged to become ViacomCBS in 2019, something of a reunion for the two companies, which had split in 2006. The streaming service CBS All Access was rebranded as Paramount+ in 2021. \r\n\r\nViacomCBS (VIACA), the company announced  the new name - Paramount - will take effect on February 16 2022 as the company celebrates Paramount+ \u2014 its streaming service, which launched in 2021.\r\n\r\nNational Amusements owns 77.3% of Paramount Global\u2019s Class A (voting) common stock and 5.2% of the Class B common stock, constituting about 10% of the overall equity of the company.\r\n\r\nParamount Global\u2019s market value was below $8 billion as of October 2023. It also has about $16 billion in long-term debt. Shari Redstone has recently dabbled around the edges, shedding some assets, such as book publisher Simon & Schuster, and engaging in talks to sell a majority stake in cable network BET.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n", "website": null, "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2026-02-18T08:32:58Z", "start_date": "2005-12-31", "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "160407", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["IRS EIN 20-3515052", "New Viacom Corp.", "Paramount", "Paramount Global", "Viacom", "Viacom Inc.", "ViacomCBS"], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Private Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "Viacom", "name_nick": null, "employees": null, "revenue": 13495500000, "fedspending_id": "332240", "lda_registrant_id": "40032"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}}, "tags": []}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/192-Paramount_Global"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 182, "attributes": {"id": 182, "name": "ViacomCBS Inc.", "blurb": "Broadcasting, cable and publishing", "summary": "ViacomCBS Inc. is comprised of the following segments: TV Entertainment (CBS Television Network, CBS Television Studios, CBS Television Distribution, CBS Interactive, CBS Sports Network, CBS Television Stations and CBS-branded streaming services), Cable Networks (Showtime Networks, Nickelodeon, MTV, BET, Comedy Central, Paramount Network, Nick Jr., VH1, TV Land, CMT, Pop TV, Smithsonian Networks, ViacomCBS Networks International, Network 10, Channel 5, Telefe and Pluto TV), Filmed Entertainment (Paramount Pictures, Paramount Players, Paramount Animation and Paramount Television Studios) and Publishing (Simon & Schuster).", "website": "https://www.viacbs.com/", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2025-10-15T21:59:11Z", "start_date": null, "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "3667,3668", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["CBS", "CBS Corporation", "CBS, Inc.", "IRS EIN 04-2949533", "ViacomCBS Inc."], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "CBS", "name_nick": null, "employees": null, "revenue": 14072900000, "fedspending_id": "59705", "lda_registrant_id": "8555"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "viac", "sec_cik": 813828}}, "tags": []}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/182-ViacomCBS_Inc."}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 43484, "attributes": {"id": 43484, "name": "AOL", "blurb": "Internet and media company", "summary": null, "website": null, "parent_id": 50, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2021-12-26T23:45:06Z", "start_date": null, "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "160325", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["AOL", "America Online Inc.", "Aol.", "Quantum Computer Services"], "types": ["Organization", "Business"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "AOL", "name_nick": null, "employees": null, "revenue": null, "fedspending_id": null, "lda_registrant_id": null}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}}, "tags": []}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/43484-AOL"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 160934, "attributes": {"id": 160934, "name": "K